{"text": " I think it's going to sound weird to say but it wasn't a very hard decision at all. Of course I love my sports and I'm going to definitely miss it. I'm not saying I'm walking away with so much resentfulness towards it. I loved every single moment of it and I think especially like last night with that battle it just made me love it even more and it's like oh then you second guess your decision but no I think I'm really at peace. I gave 22 years for the sport. My family has given 22 years for Tatjana with swimming so it really changed every dynamic and like our family and stuff and to now experience life with family and life outside of swimming is going to be so different and I'm so excited and like I said swimming was just what I did it wasn't who I am it was a season and I'm very grateful to be sitting here ending off my season in a way that I do. I know a lot of athletes can't really say that so I am very humbled and grateful to be sitting in a position where I am and yeah I think I was at peace and yeah I'm walking away with a smile. Scott I thought maybe it's important that I am the one who opens president because Okas is a very special month in South Africa. I don't have any regrets I think we always say it's such a sacrifice but it was really not a sacrifice I got to do what I love every single day I got people to dream with me and when I was down people still kept on dreaming and hoping for me and yeah I'm just grateful that I was able to achieve some of the goals that I set out but I'm excited to have new goals that don't involve swimming and to see where life takes me. People on days to mate are South Africans and we come with much smaller groups and smaller teams and stuff but our results are way better than the rest so we don't need much to do well. I was even saying in the bus you sitting there and then you have the video analysis guy the technical guy the biokinetics and here we are coach pool manager let's go and we take it on we don't need t